{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor consistently treated this as a high-risk cardiology admission, established bedside escalation rules, prevented unsupervised use of old medicines, and built a traceable discharge-medication reconciliation plan. However, the doctor prescribed unsupported numeric fluid and urine thresholds—“1000~1500ml以内” and “全天加起来不到500ml”—despite unavailable renal, electrolyte, and hemodynamic data; the ward nurse later corrected this. That minor/moderate RC5 execution error deterministically caps the trajectory at grade 2 despite later mitigation and completed higher-order verification and caregiver-workflow work.",
